Title: Fit a window larger than the screen
Repository: love
Base: def245102c67909f9902095af613b1ae05249b62
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-20
Author: aros-loeve project
Problem: Many games ask for a window larger than an AROS screen (1280x720 on an 800x600 Workbench). The window was cut off or lay partly outside the screen, with its title bar out of reach, and the game drew and read the pointer for an area that was not shown.
Change: On AROS a window that does not fit is opened as large as the screen allows (usable display bounds minus the window borders) with the proportions asked for. The game keeps the size it asked for: the difference is reported as a DPI scale below 1, so drawing, the pointer position and love.graphics.getDimensions stay in the game's units. love.window.setMode is handled the same way, and a request that fits ends the scaling. Fullscreen is not changed.
Scope: AROS (all targets); needs aros-sdl patch 0013 (SDL_SetWindowSize, SDL_SyncWindow, usable bounds)
Upstream: local-only
Verification: mainline x86_64 (nightly 2026-11-15, 800x600 screen, softpipe), 2026-11-20: a test game asking for 1280x720 gets a 780x438 window on the screen, love.graphics.getDimensions 1280x720, DPI scale 0.6083, and a click in the lower right corner arrives as 1254,690; setMode(640, 360) gives 640x360 at scale 1, setMode(1600, 1200) gives 729x547. Mr. Rescue (768x600) and SNKRX (800x600) open whole; SNKRX accepts a press on its menu. Before: graphics 1280x720 drawn into a 780x565 window 240 pixels left of the screen. Not run: Raspberry Pi, a resizable window dragged by the user, fullscreen.
Removal: not planned; AROS screens stay smaller than what desktop games expect
---
diff --git a/src/modules/window/sdl/Window.cpp b/src/modules/window/sdl/Window.cpp
index 49899d3638ac51cf2cdaaaf0cb4cb32978fb4752..531f54221b1133f6776ea003a31f99795c12eb57 100644
--- a/src/modules/window/sdl/Window.cpp
+++ b/src/modules/window/sdl/Window.cpp
@@ -635,6 +635,13 @@ bool Window::setWindow(int width, int height, WindowSettings *settings)
 	// Make sure the mouse keeps its previous grab setting.
 	setMouseGrab(mouseGrabbed);
 
+#ifdef LOVE_AROS
+	if (f.fullscreen)
+		fitScale = 1.0;
+	else
+		fitWindowToScreen(width, height);
+#endif
+
 	if (this->settings.displayindex != f.displayindex || f.useposition || f.centered)
 		SDL_SetWindowPosition(window, x, y);
 
@@ -704,6 +711,52 @@ bool Window::setWindow(int width, int height, WindowSettings *settings)
 	return true;
 }
 
+#ifdef LOVE_AROS
+void Window::fitWindowToScreen(int width, int height)
+{
+	// A screen cannot be larger than its display mode, and a window that
+	// does not fit is cut off or lies partly outside the screen. Open the
+	// window as large as the screen allows, with the game's proportions, and
+	// let the game keep the size it asked for: the difference is reported as
+	// a DPI scale below 1, which scales drawing and pointer positions.
+	fitScale = 1.0;
+
+	SDL_Rect bounds = {};
+	SDL_DisplayID display = SDL_GetDisplayForWindow(window);
+	if (width <= 0 || height <= 0)
+		return;
+	if (!SDL_GetDisplayUsableBounds(display, &bounds) && !SDL_GetDisplayBounds(display, &bounds))
+		return;
+
+	int top = 0, left = 0, bottom = 0, right = 0;
+	SDL_GetWindowBordersSize(window, &top, &left, &bottom, &right);
+
+	int availw = bounds.w - left - right;
+	int availh = bounds.h - top - bottom;
+
+	if (availw <= 0 || availh <= 0 || (width <= availw && height <= availh))
+		return;
+
+	double scale = std::min((double) availw / (double) width, (double) availh / (double) height);
+	int w = std::max(1, (int) (width * scale));
+	int h = std::max(1, (int) (height * scale));
+
+	SDL_SetWindowSize(window, w, h);
+	SDL_SyncWindow(window);
+
+	int gotw = 0, goth = 0;
+	SDL_GetWindowSize(window, &gotw, &goth);
+	if (gotw <= 0 || goth <= 0 || (gotw >= width && goth >= height))
+		return;
+
+	fitScale = std::min((double) gotw / (double) width, (double) goth / (double) height);
+	fitPixelWidth = gotw;
+	fitPixelHeight = goth;
+	fitWidth = width;
+	fitHeight = height;
+}
+#endif
+
 bool Window::onSizeChanged(int width, int height)
 {
 	if (!window)
@@ -1397,7 +1450,11 @@ void Window::DPIToWindowCoords(double *x, double *y) const
 
 double Window::getDPIScale() const
 {
+#ifdef LOVE_AROS
+	return (settings.usedpiscale ? getNativeDPIScale() : 1.0) * fitScale;
+#else
 	return settings.usedpiscale ? getNativeDPIScale() : 1.0;
+#endif
 }
 
 double Window::getNativeDPIScale() const
@@ -1428,6 +1485,15 @@ double Window::fromPixels(double x) const
 
 void Window::fromPixels(double px, double py, double &wx, double &wy) const
 {
+#ifdef LOVE_AROS
+	// The whole shrunk window is exactly the size the game asked for.
+	if (fitScale < 1.0 && px == (double) fitPixelWidth && py == (double) fitPixelHeight)
+	{
+		wx = fitWidth;
+		wy = fitHeight;
+		return;
+	}
+#endif
 	double scale = getDPIScale();
 	wx = px / scale;
 	wy = py / scale;
